{"title": "NeuroLock & Hardware Security | Berkay Özbek", "children": [{"tag": "section", "attrs": {"class": "project-hero container"}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "back", "href": "/#research"}, "children": ["← Research portfolio"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "eyebrow"}, "children": ["PHD RESEARCH / HARDWARE SECURITY"]}, {"tag": "h1", "attrs": {}, "children": ["NeuroLock: adaptable true randomness."]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "lead"}, "children": ["Adaptable true randomness and autonomous programming circuits for energy-constrained devices — extended into a portable USB-C entropy demonstrator."]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "project-meta"}, "children": [{"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["180 nm CMOS"]}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["IEEE SSCL 2025 · TVLSI 2026"]}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["ISCAS 2026 live demonstration"]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "actions"}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "text-link", "href": "https://doi.org/10.1109/LSSC.2025.3621413", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["TRNG paper ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "text-link", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=68", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["Thesis chapter 3 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "container project-content"}, "children": [{"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "metric-band"}, "children": [{"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "metric"}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["168 nW"]}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Minimum measured power"]}, {"tag": "small", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Low-power mode"]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "metric"}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["44.3 Mb/s"]}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Maximum measured throughput"]}, {"tag": "small", "attrs": {}, "children": ["High-performance mode"]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "metric"}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["3.95 pJ/bit"]}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Best measured energy efficiency"]}, {"tag": "small", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Low-power mode"]}]}]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "table-note"}, "children": ["These values describe different operating points of the same adaptable architecture."]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "story-intro"}, "children": [{"tag": "h2", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Two entropy-generation modes in one architecture"]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Wireless devices cannot assume a fixed energy budget. I developed an entropy source that can support very low-power operation and faster bursts of random-bit generation by changing the physical behaviour of its ring-oscillator delay cells."]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Low-power mode uses current-starved, slew-limited timing jitter. High-performance mode uses uncertainty in latch regeneration time. Both modes share the sampling and XOR extraction structure, keeping the output interface consistent."]}]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "figure-pair"}, "children": [{"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/trng-silicon.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "The fabricated adaptable TRNG", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: The fabricated adaptable TRNG"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/trng-silicon.webp", "width": "2200", "height": "1198", "alt": "The fabricated adaptable TRNG", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The fabricated adaptable TRNG"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The 180-nm prototype has an active area of 265 × 490 µm². The measured entropy source supports both operating regimes."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=83", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 3.5 · p. 67 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/trng-architecture.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "Mode-specific entropy, shared extraction", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: Mode-specific entropy, shared extraction"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/trng-architecture.webp", "width": "1123", "height": "1135", "alt": "Mode-specific entropy, shared extraction", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Mode-specific entropy, shared extraction"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Randomness is generated in the oscillator stages. The output sampling interface is clocked with margin rather than relying on marginal output-register metastability."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=75", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 3.2 · p. 59 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "section", "attrs": {"class": "content-section"}, "children": [{"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "eyebrow"}, "children": ["MEASURED ENTROPY & ROBUSTNESS"]}, {"tag": "h2", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Silicon measurements and statistical evaluation"]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/trng-power.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "Measured power–throughput trade-offs", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: Measured power–throughput trade-offs"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/trng-power.webp", "width": "2004", "height": "1188", "alt": "Measured power–throughput trade-offs", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Measured power–throughput trade-offs"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Mode and bias selection span nanowatt-class LP operation and high-throughput HP operation. The plot keeps power, throughput and energy-per-bit at their corresponding operating points."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=86", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 3.10 · p. 70 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "table-wrap", "tabindex": "0", "role": "region", "aria-label": "TRNG evaluation summary"}, "children": [{"tag": "table", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "caption", "attrs": {}, "children": ["TRNG evaluation summary"]}, {"tag": "thead", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "col"}, "children": ["Evaluation"]}, {"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "col"}, "children": ["Reported evidence"]}, {"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "col"}, "children": ["Conditions / interpretation"]}]}]}, {"tag": "tbody", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "row"}, "children": ["Silicon variation"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Five chips"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Output balance within ±0.07% of 50/50 using 20-Mbit datasets per chip."]}]}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "row"}, "children": ["Temperature sweep"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["−20 to 80 °C"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Both modes characterised using 20-Mbit datasets per point."]}]}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "row"}, "children": ["Statistical testing"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["NIST SP 800-22, SP 800-90B and AIS31"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["100-Mbit datasets for the reported nominal test batteries; see thesis Tables 3.1–3.3 for individual results."]}]}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "row"}, "children": ["Supply-injection test"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["SP 800-22 pass up to 400 mV"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["HP mode at the sensitive injected frequency around 6.96 MHz; no external filtering capacitors."]}]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "table-note"}, "children": ["These are reported experimental test results, not a claim of independent certification. Statistical tests support characterisation and do not alone establish security for every application."]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/trng-injection.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "Testing a sensitive supply-injection condition", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: Testing a sensitive supply-injection condition"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/trng-injection.webp", "width": "1400", "height": "600", "alt": "Testing a sensitive supply-injection condition", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Testing a sensitive supply-injection condition"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The amplitude sweep evaluates deliberate ripple near an oscillator harmonic. The reported NIST SP 800-22 pass extends through 400 mV; the more extreme 600 mV condition shows degradation."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=90", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 3.16 · p. 74 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "section", "attrs": {"id": "demonstrator", "class": "content-section demo-story"}, "children": [{"tag": "div", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "eyebrow"}, "children": ["SILICON TO APPLICATION"]}, {"tag": "h2", "attrs": {}, "children": ["A USB-C TRNG with an interactive application"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The USB-C demonstrator connects the TRNG chip to a XIAO RP2040 and streams raw output bytes over USB serial. A Python GUI monitors and uses the incoming stream, making the connection between physical entropy and application behaviour visible."]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The thesis documents key/seed provisioning, messaging integrity, signing, re-keying and file protection. The later NeuroLock GUI extends the experience to generative art, terrain, Monte Carlo visualisation, lottery draws, aleatoric music and neural-implant demonstrations."]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "table-note"}, "children": ["The live GUI is a host application connected to the chip. Its health indicators are monitoring tools; the website does not substitute browser-generated randomness for the TRNG stream."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "text-link", "href": "https://doi.org/10.1109/ISCAS66217.2026.11562525", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["ISCAS live demonstration ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/neurolock-demo.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "The real USB-C demonstrator", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: The real USB-C demonstrator"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/neurolock-demo.webp", "width": "1857", "height": "1690", "alt": "The real USB-C demonstrator", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The real USB-C demonstrator"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Photo from the PhD thesis appendix, showing the compact TRNG hardware and host interface."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=196", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. A.1 · p. 180 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "section", "attrs": {"class": "content-section"}, "children": [{"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "eyebrow"}, "children": ["AUTONOMOUS PROGRAMMING"]}, {"tag": "h2", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Closed-loop OTP programming control"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "prose"}, "children": ["The programming controller searches voltage and pulse-duration candidates instead of relying on one fixed worst-case recipe. A current-threshold crossing stops the charge-pump clock and captures the voltage/time code. Explicit discharge between attempts establishes a repeatable starting condition."]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "figure-pair"}, "children": [{"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/otp-controller.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "The 180-nm programming-controller prototype", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: The 180-nm programming-controller prototype"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/otp-controller.webp", "width": "2200", "height": "1089", "alt": "The 180-nm programming-controller prototype", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The 180-nm programming-controller prototype"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["High-voltage charge pump, DAC, current-trip circuits and controller integrated for closed-loop parameter extraction."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=111", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 3.24 · p. 95 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/otp-search.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "Measured voltage–time search", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: Measured voltage–time search"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/otp-search.webp", "width": "2200", "height": "1379", "alt": "Measured voltage–time search", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Measured voltage–time search"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The controller steps through approximately 5.2–12.5 V and escalates stress-window duration between sweeps. Full-cycle average power is 363 µW during this one-time characterisation operation."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=112", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 3.25 · p. 96 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "aside", "attrs": {"class": "evidence-note"}, "children": [{"tag": "h3", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Controller validation and memory integration"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The intended 1-kbit antifuse array was functionally simulated, but reliable on-chip programming/readout was not achieved in the prototype. Controller measurements therefore used externally emulated current transitions to validate candidate sequencing, event detection and pump shutdown. Reliable embedded nonvolatile storage remains an integration objective."]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "actions"}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "text-link", "href": "https://doi.org/10.1109/TVLSI.2026.3706590", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["Programming-controller paper ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "text-link", "href": "/neurostreamx"}, "children": ["See credential-gated telemetry ↗"]}]}]}]}]}